 ## Overview
-Incremental Registration is a training strategy for joint pose and radiance field optimization that registers camera frames sequentially following their temporal order [S2]. It solves the problem of non-convex pose optimization and local minima by leveraging the intuition that adjacent camera poses in video sequences are spatially close [S2]. Unlike methods that optimize all poses simultaneously or rely on global initialization, this method incrementally adds frames to the training buffer, initializing new poses from previous ones and freezing older parameters to prevent disruption [S2]. Builds on [Progressive and Dynamic Scene Growth](8869-progressive-and-dynamic-scene-growth.md).
